[agent:result]     Note: Lazy
[agent:result]         This method is lazy and does not persist any metadata or feature data in the feature store on its own.
[agent:result]         To persist the feature group and save feature data along the metadata in the feature store, call the `save()` method with a DataFrame.
[agent:result] 
[agent:result]     Parameters:
[agent:result]         name: Name of the feature group to create.
[agent:result]         version: Version of the feature group to create, defaults to `None` and will create the feature group with incremented version from the last version in the feature store.
[agent:result]         description: A string describing the contents of the feature group to improve discoverability for Data Scientists.
[agent:result]         online_enabled: Define whether the feature group should be made available also in the online feature store for low latency access.
[agent:result]         time_travel_format: Format used for time travel, either `"DELTA"`, `"HUDI"`, or `None` to disable time travel, defaults to `"DELTA"`.
[agent:result]         partition_key: A list of feature names to be used as partition key when writing the feature data to the offline storage, defaults to empty list `[]`.
[agent:result]         primary_key:
[agent:result]             A list of feature names to be used as primary key for the feature group.
[agent:result]             This primary key can be a composite key of multiple features and will be used as joining key, if not specified otherwise.
[agent:result]             Defaults to empty list `[]`, and the feature group won't have any primary key.
[agent:result]         foreign_key:
[agent:result]             A list of feature names to be used as foreign key for the feature group.
[agent:result]             Foreign key is referencing the primary key of another feature group and can be used as joining key.
[agent:result]             Defaults to empty list `[]`, and the feature group won't have any foreign key.
[agent:result]         embedding_index:
[agent:result]             [`EmbeddingIndex`][hsfs.embedding.EmbeddingIndex]. If an embedding index is provided, vector database is used as online feature store.
[agent:result]             This enables similarity search by using [`FeatureGroup.find_neighbors`][hsfs.feature_group.FeatureGroup.find_neighbors].
[agent:result]         hudi_precombine_key:
[agent:result]             A feature name to be used as a precombine key for the `"HUDI"` feature group.
[agent:result]             If feature group has time travel format `"HUDI"` and hudi precombine key was not specified then the first primary key of the feature group will be used as hudi precombine key.
[agent:result]         features:
[agent:result]             Optionally, define the schema of the feature group manually as a list of `Feature` objects.
[agent:result]             Defaults to empty list `[]` and will use the schema information of the DataFrame provided in the `save` method.
[agent:result]         statistics_config:
[agent:result]             A configuration object, or a dictionary with keys:
[agent:result] 
[agent:result]             - `enabled` to generally enable descriptive statistics computation for this feature group,
[agent:result]             - `correlations` to turn on feature correlation computation,
[agent:result]             - `histograms` to compute feature value frequencies, and
[agent:result]             - `exact_uniqueness` to compute uniqueness, distinctness and entropy.
[agent:result] 
[agent:result]             The values should be booleans indicating the setting.
[agent:result]             To fully turn off statistics computation pass `statistics_config=False`.
[agent:result]             By default, it computes only descriptive statistics.
[agent:result]         event_time:
[agent:result]             Optionally, provide the name of the feature containing the event time for the features in this feature group.
[agent:result]             If event_time is set the feature group can be used for point-in-time joins.
[agent:result] 
[agent:result]             Note: Event time data type restriction
[agent:result]                 The supported data types for the event time column are: `timestamp`, `date` and `bigint`.
[agent:result] 
[agent:result]         stream:
[agent:result]             Optionally, define whether the feature group should support real time stream writing capabilities.
[agent:result]             Stream enabled Feature Groups have unified single API for writing streaming features transparently to both online and offline store.
[agent:result]         expectation_suite:
[agent:result]             Optionally, attach an expectation suite to the feature group which dataframes should be validated against upon insertion.
[agent:result]         parents:
[agent:result]             Optionally, define the parents of this feature group as the origin where the data is coming from.
[agent:result]         topic_name:
[agent:result]             Optionally, define the name of the topic used for data ingestion.
[agent:result]             If left undefined it defaults to using project topic.
[agent:result]         notification_topic_name:
[agent:result]             Optionally, define the name of the topic used for sending notifications when entries are inserted or updated on the online feature store.
[agent:result]             If left undefined no notifications are sent.
[agent:result]         transformation_functions:
[agent:result]             On-Demand Transformation functions attached to the feature group.
[agent:result]             It can be a list of list of user defined functions defined using the hopsworks `@udf` decorator.
[agent:result]             Defaults to `None`, no transformations.
[agent:result]         online_config:
[agent:result]             Optionally, configure the underlying RonDB online table.
[agent:result]             Accepts an [`OnlineConfig`][hsfs.online_config.OnlineConfig] instance or a dictionary with snake_case keys (e.g. `{"primary_key_index_type": "HASH"}`).
[agent:result] 
[agent:result]             Recognized fields:
[agent:result] 
[agent:result]             - `online_comments`: List of RonDB `COMMENT` directives applied to the table (e.g. `NDB_TABLE=READ_BACKUP=1`).
[agent:result]             - `table_space`: Name of the RonDB tablespace for on-disk storage.
[agent:result]               Overridden by `online_disk=True`.
[agent:result]             - `primary_key_index_type`: Primary key index shape — `"HASH"` (hash-only, fastest point lookups), `"ORDERED"` (hash + ordered indexes, supports both point lookups and range scans), or unset.
[agent:result]               Left unset, a TTL-driven default is applied: `"HASH"` when TTL is disabled, hash + ordered when TTL is enabled so the TTL cleaner can range-scan by event time.
[agent:result]               See [`OnlineConfig.primary_key_index_type`][hsfs.online_config.OnlineConfig.primary_key_index_type] for full per-value guidance.
[agent:result]               Set at feature group creation time only — cannot be changed after the table exists.
